# ordinal: preferred target, alternates, aliases, corpus-earned opening,
# evidence synthesis, Zen bend / scope statement.
S={
851:("take a staff-blow",["receive a blow"],["take a beating","receive the staff","get hit","staff blow"],"To take a staff-blow is to become the recipient of a recorded strike, whether threatened, prescribed, or actually delivered in an encounter.","The cases use the phrase after failed answers, in warnings about what a participant deserves, and in comments that reverse who should receive the blow.","The ordinary result of being hit becomes a public verdict whose target and timing must be read from each exchange."),
852:("garden steward",["monastery garden officer"],["garden steward","garden officer","monastery gardener","vegetable garden officer"],"The garden steward is the monastery officer charged with cultivated grounds and their produce.","Rules and encounter records place the officer among the rotating work offices and show the holder meeting teachers while carrying out garden business.","A labor title becomes an accountable community office and, in recorded meetings, a participant rather than scenery."),
853:("gain insight at the words",["awaken upon hearing the words"],["insight at the words","awaken on hearing","understand at his words","hearing breakthrough"],"To gain insight at the words is a narrated turn in which a listener's understanding changes at a particular utterance.","Biographical passages attach the event to an immediately preceding saying and distinguish it from later full awakening when the record does so.","The phrase binds a change in understanding to a public spoken turn without making the words a repeatable technique."),
854:("secretary",["recording secretary"],["secretary","monastic secretary","recording officer","scribe"],"The secretary is a monastery office whose holder writes, records, or manages formal correspondence and can also appear as an interlocutor.","The witnesses use the title in appointments, authorship notices, administrative lists, and named encounters.","The writing office enters Zen evidence both through preservation of records and through its holder's public exchanges."),
855:("rice steward",["meal-grain officer"],["rice steward","meal officer","rice head","monastery kitchen officer"],"The rice steward is the monastery officer responsible for the community's rice and meal provisioning.","Rules list the office among material duties, while biographies and cases identify individual holders encountered at work.","A kitchen duty becomes a named institutional position whose holder can be questioned and answer publicly."),
856:("a phrase that meets the occasion",["the occasion-matching phrase"],["timely phrase","phrase at the occasion","fitting response","live answer"],"A phrase that meets the occasion is an answer required to fit the live demand of the exchange in which it is spoken.","Teachers ask for it, deny that a supplied line qualifies, or present a line whose adequacy the next turn tests.","The phrase is not a maxim stored in advance: its fit is exposed only in the public exchange."),
857:("head-on",["right at the head"],["head on","directly before one","immediate blow","face to face"],"Head-on marks something delivered or encountered directly at the decisive point, especially a blow, rebuke, or obstruction.","The selected predicates put blows, shouts, and barriers immediately before a participant rather than describing an abstract direction.","The spatial adverb sharpens the immediacy of a public encounter; it does not itself name one fixed device."),
858:("Master Zhuang",["Zhuangzi"],["Zhuangzi","Master Zhuang","Zhuang Zhou text","Daoist author"],"Master Zhuang is the named pre-Chan author and case figure whose sayings, dreams, and images Chan speakers quote and contest.","The records invoke his butterfly, fish, skill stories, and attributed words inside addresses and comments rather than supplying a detached biography.","He is defined here by Zen deployment: a repeatedly raised speaker and story-source made answerable in later public discourse."),
859:("the matter at the edge of the teaching-body",["what lies beside the embodiment of the teaching"],["teaching body edge","beyond the teaching body","matter beside the teaching body","boundary question"],"The matter at the edge of the teaching-body is a stock interview question asking what remains to be said or done at that asserted boundary.","Different teachers answer it with fresh lines, and later compilers raise those answers as cases rather than harmonizing them.","An inherited body-term is bent into the location of a live question whose answer belongs to its exchange."),
860:("skilled hand",["expert"],["skilled hand","expert operator","capable person","master hand"],"A skilled hand is a person whose command is visible in handling a case, object, verse, or encounter.","Speakers praise, challenge, or ironically withhold the label according to an observable performance in the surrounding passage.","The craft compliment becomes an appraisal of public handling, but the local verdict may be praise or criticism."),
861:("provide a meal for the monastic assembly",["feast the monastics"],["feed monks","monastic meal offering","provide assembly meal","sponsor a meal"],"To provide a meal for the monastic assembly is a public act of sponsorship recorded as the occasion for an address or gathering.","Invitations and discourse headings name the sponsor and meal, while rules place the event in the community's collective schedule.","Food provision becomes the documented occasion of public teaching without ceasing to be a material meal."),
862:("a phrase",["one saying"],["one phrase","single saying","give a phrase","one line answer"],"A phrase is a bounded verbal turn demanded, offered, or judged in a Chan exchange.","The witnesses ask someone to produce it, distinguish first and second phrases, or test whether a line can carry the matter at hand.","The diminutive does not make the answer trivial: it isolates one public turn for immediate judgment."),
863:("Vairocana",["Lushena Buddha"],["Vairocana","Lushena","cosmic Buddha","Vairocana figure"],"Vairocana is the Buddha figure whom Chan speakers invoke through the broad body, tongue, crown, or teaching-seat images attached to his name.","Addresses place him in comparisons and questions and sometimes set his body against the immediate words or actions of the hall.","This Buddha is defined by those Zen deployments, not by an imported comprehensive hagiography."),
864:("the patriarch's meaning",["the ancestral teacher's intent"],["patriarch meaning","ancestral intent","meaning of Bodhidharma","patriarch's purpose"],"The patriarch's meaning is a recurrent public-interview demand for what the ancestral transmission amounts to here.","The corpus preserves incompatible object-answers, verbal answers, refusals, and later comments under the same question.","Zen bends the historical inquiry into a live test and does not reduce the varied answers to one hidden proposition."),
865:("infirmary hall",["monastery sick hall"],["infirmary","sick hall","nirvana hall","monastery hospice"],"The infirmary hall is the monastery place assigned to sick or dying residents and governed by communal rules.","Regulations describe its officers and provisions, while biographies locate final exchanges and deaths there.","The auspicious name enters Zen as a concrete institution where care and last public words are recorded."),
866:("Zhenzhou radishes",["the radishes of Zhenzhou"],["Zhenzhou radish","Zhaozhou radish case","radish answer","turnip case"],"Zhenzhou radishes are Zhaozhou's local-produce answer, later remembered and tested as a named case.","Later teachers pair the answer with Zhaozhou's tea, ask after its taste, or criticize attempts to explain it away.","An ordinary regional vegetable becomes a portable case while remaining the concrete answer actually given."),
867:("acceptance of the unborn under the staff",["unborn acceptance beneath a blow"],["staff unborn acceptance","blow and no birth","Linji staff phrase","awakening under staff"],"Acceptance of the unborn under the staff is a later formula joining a staff-blow to the claimed realization received there.","The records quote, verse, and question the formula, frequently alongside Linji's shout and Deshan's staff.","The inherited attainment term is tied to a violent public encounter, but the entry does not turn striking into a universal method."),
868:("bring a person to life",["a life-giving person"],["bring alive","revive a person","living person","life giving response"],"To bring a person to life is the restorative side of an encounter vocabulary that contrasts killing and enlivening.","Speakers ask for a life-giving phrase, praise a response as bringing someone alive, or contrast it with a deadening handling.","Life and death become appraisals of what a public turn does, not medical claims about a corpse."),
869:("Mahasthamaprapta",["Bodhisattva Great Strength"],["Mahasthamaprapta","Great Strength bodhisattva","Seishi","Bodhisattva of power"],"Mahasthamaprapta is a pre-Chan figure invoked by name in quotations, images, and comparisons used by Zen speakers.","The witnesses place the figure in teaching assemblies and inherited narratives that masters raise for their own audience.","The entry defines the figure through that Zen deployment rather than importing a complete devotional identity."),
870:("staffs and shouts fly back and forth",["blows and shouts cross"],["staff and shout","blows shouts exchange","Linji Deshan devices","staff shout contest"],"Staffs and shouts flying back and forth describes rapid reciprocal use of the two emblematic encounter devices.","Addresses use the formula for exchanges in which striking and shouting answer one another, and later comments judge whether such display has life.","The paired devices become public-interview traffic, not a generic synonym for violence or noise."),
871:("black-lacquer bucket",["pitch-black bucket"],["lacquer bucket","black bucket insult","blind fool","dark bucket"],"A black-lacquer bucket is a blunt address for someone presented as unable to distinguish what is directly before them.","Teachers apply it after failed recognitions, circular signs, or answers, and later commentators repeat it as an encounter verdict.","The dark container becomes a person-directed rebuke; the corpus does not establish a diagnostic inner state beyond each failure."),
872:("the Brahmin wanderer",["Brahmin ascetic"],["Brahmin","wanderer","Indian ascetic","Brahmin case figure"],"The Brahmin wanderer is a pre-Chan case figure who questions, visits, or acts before a Buddha or master in inherited stories raised by Zen speakers.","The witnesses preserve distinct wanderers and episodes, so the social label does not identify one biography.","Zen deploys the figure as a named role within cases; each occurrence must retain its local actor and story."),
873:("ascend the teaching hall",["mount the hall seat"],["ascend hall","formal address","take teaching seat","enter dharma hall"],"To ascend the teaching hall is the formal act by which an abbot takes the public teaching position before the assembly.","Records use it to open questions, sermons, appointments, commemorations, and other named occasions.","Movement into a hall becomes the institutional threshold of a public interview or address."),
874:("the second phrase",["the second line"],["second phrase","second statement","three phrases","Linji second phrase"],"The second phrase is a ranked or sequential verbal position whose force depends on the local first-and-third-phrase scheme.","Teachers ask what it is, supply contrasting lines, and criticize people who remain at that level.","An ordinal becomes house vocabulary for judging speech, but the records do not supply one universal sentence as its content."),
875:("rear hall",["rear-hall office"],["rear hall","second seat","rear hall master","monastery hall"],"The rear hall is both a monastery space and, in office titles, the teaching position associated with that hall.","Rules assign seating and duties to its officer, while records identify named rear-hall teachers and encounters.","Room and office are different things and are separated when the exact predicates establish which is meant."),
876:("at the tip of the staff",["under the staff's head"],["staff tip","under the blow","staff point","at the staff"],"At the tip of the staff locates the decisive point of a blow or the claimed activity displayed through the staff.","The witnesses ask for life, an eye, or a turning at that point and judge what appears when the implement is used.","A physical tip becomes the exposed point of public testing without turning the staff into a purely abstract symbol."),
877:("chief monastic administrator",["sangha director"],["chief monastic","monastic registrar","sangha administrator","clerical office"],"The chief monastic administrator is an official rank responsible for oversight of ordained communities or monasteries.","Titles, appointments, petitions, and biographies name holders of the office, sometimes as patrons or interlocutors.","The bureaucratic title enters Zen records through institutional authority, not as a synonym for a teaching master."),
878:("fully raise the true command",["bring forth the command in full"],["true command","full command","raise the order","complete authority"],"To fully raise the true command is to bring the teaching-seat's directive authority into the open without partial handling.","Addresses pair the formula with staffs, shouts, questions, and judgments about whether the occasion has actually been met.","Military command language becomes an appraisal of public authority while remaining answerable to the recorded response."),
879:("recognize it here",["take it up here"],["recognize this","see it here","take it directly","discern now"],"To recognize it here is a direct imperative asking the listener to identify what the present words or scene already put forward.","Teachers attach it to visible objects, immediate questions, and lines just spoken, and the following turn shows whether recognition was claimed.","The ordinary recognition verb becomes a pointed public demand, not an instruction for a private exercise."),
880:("Lingyun sees peach blossoms",["Lingyun's peach-blossom awakening"],["Lingyun peach blossoms","seeing peach flowers","Lingyun Zhiqin case","peach blossom case"],"Lingyun seeing peach blossoms is the named case in which Lingyun Zhiqin reports awakening at the sight of spring flowers.","Later teachers quote his verse, question the sight, and compare or criticize what was gained without erasing the narrated event.","A visual biographical turn becomes a public case whose later uses are part of its Zen identity."),
881:("guest within the guest",["guest in the guest position"],["guest within guest","four guests hosts","guest position","Linji guest host"],"Guest within the guest is one position in the fourfold guest-host vocabulary, commonly answered by a scene or action rather than a definition.","Question sequences ask for all four positions, and later addresses use the category to assess how an interlocutor stands.","Nested social roles become technical interview positions, but each recorded answer remains local evidence rather than a universal paraphrase."),
882:("Chan visitor",["visiting Chan monastic"],["Chan visitor","visiting monk","travelling Zen monk","guest monastic"],"A Chan visitor is a travelling monastic who comes to question, stay, or seek an encounter at the presiding master's community.","Rules govern reception and records show visitors entering the hall, asking questions, and being assigned lodging.","The ordinary guest is institutionally the mobile participant through whom many public interviews begin."),
883:("head seat",["senior seat"],["head seat","chief monk","senior monastic","first seat"],"The head seat is the senior monastic office immediately visible in the teaching hall and community hierarchy.","Rules define its seating and duties, while records show holders answering for the assembly, being appointed, or entering exchanges.","Rank becomes a public responsibility; the title does not automatically make its holder the utterer of every surrounding line."),
884:("the World-Honored One remained silent",["the Buddha paused at length"],["Buddha silent","World Honored One pause","long silence case","Buddha remained silent"],"The World-Honored One remaining silent is a narrated Buddha-case turn in which an extended pause itself occupies the answer position.","Later teachers raise, verse, and criticize the silence and compare it with other wordless actions.","The Zen Buddha is defined here by his deployment in this public case; silence is the recorded turn, not a universal doctrine."),
885:("ordinary",["everyday"],["ordinary","usual","everyday","normal course"],"Ordinary names what is usual or everyday, but Chan compounds and answers repeatedly make that baseline itself the disputed matter.","The witnesses attach it to mind, speech, meals, conduct, and customary affairs, with local predicates deciding whether it is praised or rejected.","Zen bends the everyday into an interview criterion without making every ordinary occurrence one technical sense."),
886:("estate steward",["farm-estate manager"],["estate steward","farm manager","monastery estate officer","manor head"],"The estate steward manages a monastery's outlying farm or landed property and its material obligations.","Rules and biographies identify the office, and cases show its holder meeting the presiding master during estate business.","An agricultural administrator becomes a recorded institutional actor, not merely the owner of a village."),
887:("strike with the fly-whisk",["hit with the whisk"],["strike whisk","fly whisk blow","whisk teaching action","hit the whisk"],"To strike with the fly-whisk is a visible teaching-seat action directed at the seat, stand, or another point in the hall.","The records follow the strike with questions, declarations, or closure of the address, making its placement part of the public turn.","The fly-whisk is an authority-bearing teaching implement here, not a household insect tool."),
888:("Buddha Great Penetrating Wisdom Victory",["Mahabhijnajnanabhibhu Buddha"],["Great Penetrating Wisdom Victory","ancient Buddha","Daitsu Chisho","Buddha waited ten kalpas"],"Buddha Great Penetrating Wisdom Victory is the pre-Chan Buddha whom Zen speakers invoke through the ten-kalpa sitting and non-manifest awakening case.","Teachers quote the verse, ask why the way did not manifest, and turn the ancient figure into a present public question.","This Buddha is defined by that Zen case deployment rather than an outside life story."),
889:("the whole body is a mouth",["all over is a mouth"],["whole body mouth","body as speech","entire body speaks","mouth everywhere"],"The whole body being a mouth is an impossible bodily speech-image used when asking how wind, objects, or a person voices the matter without one localized organ.","The witnesses pair it with whole-body eyes or ears and demand an answer about speaking and hearing.","A bodily impossibility becomes a public question about expression; it is not resolved into an imported metaphysics."),
890:("an adept",["one capable of the work"],["adept","capable person","author of the deed","expert Chan person"],"An adept is the person judged capable of handling the live work of an encounter rather than merely repeating its vocabulary.","Speakers ask whether an adept is present, praise a particular turn, or use the label ironically when the handling fails.","Authorship language becomes an encounter appraisal whose polarity must be taken from the surrounding case."),
891:("the price of rice in Luling",["Luling's rice price"],["Luling rice price","Qingyuan rice answer","rice price case","price of rice"],"The price of rice in Luling is Qingyuan Xingsi's concrete answer to a question about the great meaning of the teaching.","Later verses preserve the market question, debate its price and freshness, and treat it as a named case without replacing the answer.","An ordinary local price becomes a portable public case while remaining the wording actually used."),
892:("the matter beyond a buddha",["what is above buddhahood"],["beyond Buddha","above Buddha matter","Buddha upward matter","what surpasses Buddha"],"The matter beyond a buddha is a stock interview question asking what can be said once even the title buddha is treated as a position to pass.","Different teachers answer with persons, objects, refusals, and reversals, and later commentators preserve the divergence.","Rank language becomes a live question; the corpus does not authorize one metaphysical object beyond all buddhas."),
893:("Mount Sumeru",["Sumeru mountain"],["Mount Sumeru","Sumeru answer","world mountain","Yunmen Sumeru"],"Mount Sumeru is both the inherited world-mountain and, in a famous Yunmen exchange, the abrupt answer later raised as a case.","The witnesses use the mountain in cosmological comparisons and repeatedly quote, verse, or question Yunmen's answer.","The physical inherited image and named answer-case are different deployments and must remain distinguishable when both are anchored."),
894:("Yan Hui",["Master Yan"],["Yan Hui","Confucius disciple","Master Yan","Hui who did not repeat faults"],"Yan Hui is the pre-Chan student figure whom Zen speakers invoke through stories of poverty, learning, and not repeating a fault.","The records quote or adapt exchanges involving Confucius and Yan Hui inside sermons and comparisons.","He is defined by those Zen deployments, not by a freestanding Confucian biography."),
895:("arrowheads meeting point to point",["two arrowpoints brace each other"],["arrowheads meet","arrow point exchange","matched responses","point to point"],"Arrowheads meeting point to point is an image for two encounter turns matching with no gap between their active points.","Commentators apply it to paired answers and exchanges, while contrasting cases expose when the apparent match misses.","The weapon image becomes a verdict on reciprocal precision, not a claim that every agreement is correct."),
896:("stone chime",["ritual chime"],["stone chime","monastery chime","qing instrument","hanging chime"],"The stone chime is a struck instrument used to signal, punctuate, or accompany monastery and ceremonial events.","Rules place it among audible signals, while cases include hearing, striking, or comparisons to its sound and shape.","A ritual instrument enters the public soundscape of Zen institutions without becoming merely a symbol."),
897:("make the upper offering",["present the principal offering"],["upper offering","principal offering","altar offering","make offerings"],"To make the upper offering is a formal presentation of food or incense at a principal altar or commemorative rite.","Ceremonial headings and regulations place it in an ordered sequence and name the officiating occasion.","The material offering belongs to the monastery's public ritual calendar, not an inferred private exercise."),
898:("announce with the white mallet",["strike the white mallet"],["white mallet","announce assembly","hall mallet","formal proclamation"],"To announce with the white mallet is the hall officer's formal signal and proclamation that frames a public assembly or debate.","Records place the mallet at the opening or close, give its spoken formula, and identify the officer who performs it.","An implement and announcement together establish public order; the mallet is not just percussion."),
899:("bell and board",["bell-and-board signals"],["bell board","monastery signals","wooden board","community schedule"],"Bell and board are paired monastery signals that announce times, movements, and communal duties.","Regulations specify when they sound and biographies use their sounding to locate events in the resident schedule.","The instruments become the audible governance of community time while remaining concrete objects."),
900:("one question, one answer",["a question-and-answer exchange"],["question answer","one exchange","public interview","question and response"],"One question and one answer is the minimal paired structure of a public interview, with each turn attributable to its own utterer.","The witnesses count or characterize exchanges, distinguish responsive pairs from mere talk, and preserve the exact question and reply.","Zen's mode is public question and answer: the pair is evidence only when both turns and their speakers remain visible."),
}

